      <Comment source="nilo-poyanco, PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">According to the nomenclature used for hybrid and complex &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycans, this compound is known as 2,2. The name is derived by having one &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosaminyl residue attached by a &amp;beta;1-2 linkage to the &amp;alpha;-Man-(1&amp;rarr;6) arm of the three mannose core, and one &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosaminyl residue attached by a &amp;beta;1-2 linkage to the &amp;alpha;-Man-(1&amp;rarr;3) arm |CITS: [24178944]|.</Comment>
